WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.629 --> 00:00:18.592
"Wow," Cole said as Nora started crying even harder.

2
00:00:18.612 --> 00:00:20.993
"It looks like we just solved the mystery."

3
00:00:21.013 --> 00:00:23.474
"Yeah," Henry agreed.

4
00:00:23.494 --> 00:00:27.335
"So my funny feeling was wrong," he thought.

5
00:00:28.155 --> 00:00:31.396
He'd been convinced that Nora was too little to be the thief.

6
00:00:32.204 --> 00:00:34.906
But now, here she was, confessing to the crime.

7
00:00:34.926 --> 00:00:37.888
"I'm sorry, Maggie!"

8
00:00:38.228 --> 00:00:40.050
Nora blurted out between sobs.

9
00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:43.292
"I didn't think you'd mind if I took it."

10
00:00:43.312 --> 00:00:45.574
"You didn't think I'd mind?"

11
00:00:46.515 --> 00:00:47.936
Maggie echoed in disbelief.

12
00:00:47.956 --> 00:00:49.757
"Are you crazy?

13
00:00:50.738 --> 00:00:52.159
Why wouldn't I mind?

14
00:00:53.039 --> 00:00:54.360
You took my money!"

15
00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:57.422
"Huh?" Nora blinked and sniffled.

16
00:00:57.442 --> 00:00:59.124
"What money?"

17
00:01:00.432 --> 00:01:03.214
"The money you grabbed from the cashbox," Cole said.

18
00:01:03.234 --> 00:01:05.936
"Those two older girls saw you take it."

19
00:01:06.897 --> 00:01:09.399
Henry was starting to get that funny feeling again.

20
00:01:09.419 --> 00:01:11.760
"Wait," he said.

21
00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:13.942
"The girls didn't say that.

22
00:01:14.883 --> 00:01:19.646
They just said they saw Nora grabbing something from the table and looking sneaky.

23
00:01:20.507 --> 00:01:21.688
What did you take, Nora?"

24
00:01:22.989 --> 00:01:25.210
"None of your business," Nora said.

25
00:01:25.851 --> 00:01:27.232
She wasn't crying anymore.

26
00:01:28.136 --> 00:01:30.297
Now she was starting to look stubborn.

27
00:01:31.198 --> 00:01:32.258
Henry stared at her.

28
00:01:33.219 --> 00:01:35.220
Something about this didn't make sense.

29
00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:38.522
He just wished he could figure out what it was.

30
00:01:38.542 --> 00:01:41.483
"You'd better tell me right now, Nora!"

31
00:01:41.763 --> 00:01:42.864
Maggie exclaimed.

32
00:01:42.884 --> 00:01:47.086
"You can't make me," Nora yelled back.

33
00:01:47.106 --> 00:01:49.688
"Yeah!" Nora's friend added.

34
00:01:49.708 --> 00:01:51.969
"You can't order her around.

35
00:01:52.829 --> 00:01:54.270
She's a princess!"

36
00:01:55.271 --> 00:01:57.572
Just then Nathan hurried out of the house.

37
00:01:58.696 --> 00:01:59.997
"What's going on out here?"

38
00:02:00.718 --> 00:02:01.338
he asked.

39
00:02:02.799 --> 00:02:04.621
"Hi, Nathan," Henry said.

40
00:02:04.641 --> 00:02:07.463
"We were just talking to your sister."

41
00:02:07.483 --> 00:02:09.544
"No, they weren't!"

42
00:02:09.864 --> 00:02:11.446
Nora started to cry again.

43
00:02:11.466 --> 00:02:16.789
"They were trying to drag me off to jail!"

44
00:02:16.809 --> 00:02:21.193
"What?" Now Nathan looked really confused.

45
00:02:22.233 --> 00:02:24.895
"She's exaggerating," Maggie said.

46
00:02:26.072 --> 00:02:28.373
"We were just trying to get my money back.

47
00:02:29.213 --> 00:02:30.354
Nora stole it!"

48
00:02:31.154 --> 00:02:32.355
Nathan shook his head.

49
00:02:32.375 --> 00:02:34.616
"Nora didn't take that money."

50
00:02:34.636 --> 00:02:38.478
"Yeah!" Nora stuck out her tongue at Maggie.

51
00:02:38.498 --> 00:02:40.879
"I didn't take your money."

52
00:02:40.899 --> 00:02:42.279
"Yes, you did!"

53
00:02:42.659 --> 00:02:43.280
Maggie said.

54
00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:46.441
"You just confessed, remember?"

55
00:02:46.461 --> 00:02:48.542
"No way."

56
00:02:49.242 --> 00:02:50.523
Nora looked stubborn again.

57
00:02:50.543 --> 00:02:52.884
"I didn't take any money.

58
00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:56.241
All I took was an extra cup of lemonade!"

59
00:02:57.001 --> 00:02:58.381
Everyone looked surprised.

60
00:02:58.401 --> 00:03:00.302
"Extra lemonade?"

61
00:03:00.642 --> 00:03:01.322
Cole said.

62
00:03:01.342 --> 00:03:04.223
"Oh Henry nodded.

63
00:03:04.243 --> 00:03:08.124
"That must be what those teenage girls saw her doing.

64
00:03:09.084 --> 00:03:11.405
Nora wasn't sneaking around to steal the money.

65
00:03:11.985 --> 00:03:14.346
She was just sneaking some extra lemonade."

66
00:03:14.366 --> 00:03:18.187
"How do we know she didn't do both things?

67
00:03:19.387 --> 00:03:22.888
She just admitted that she's a lemonade thief," Maggie said.

68
00:03:23.784 --> 00:03:25.605
"She might be a money thief too!"

69
00:03:25.625 --> 00:03:29.047
"Come on, Maggie," Nathan said.

70
00:03:29.067 --> 00:03:32.949
"Nora might be sneaky enough to grab some extra lemonade.

71
00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:35.791
But she wouldn't steal your cash."

72
00:03:37.192 --> 00:03:43.115
"Maybe not on her own," Maggie said, glancing from Nora to Nathan and then back again.

73
00:03:44.076 --> 00:03:46.377
Nathan folded his arms across his chest.

74
00:03:46.397 --> 00:03:48.098
"What do you mean?"

75
00:03:48.878 --> 00:03:49.399
he asked.

76
00:03:49.419 --> 00:03:51.300
"Cole was right.

77
00:03:52.076 --> 00:03:54.277
It was probably all your idea!"

78
00:03:54.677 --> 00:03:55.617
Maggie burst out.

79
00:03:55.637 --> 00:03:58.198
"Wait, I didn't say that!"

80
00:03:59.058 --> 00:03:59.918
Cole chimed in.

81
00:04:00.819 --> 00:04:02.799
Maggie didn't pay any attention to him.

82
00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:05.200
She was still staring at Nathan.

83
00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:12.022
"You two were wandering past and saw that I was making tons of money at my lemonade stand,"

84
00:04:12.422 --> 00:04:12.882
she said.

85
00:04:12.902 --> 00:04:15.223
"So you got greedy."

86
00:04:16.203 --> 00:04:18.104
She narrowed her eyes and looked around.

87
00:04:19.472 --> 00:04:23.115
Henry could tell she was pausing to make her story sound more dramatic.

88
00:04:24.076 --> 00:04:26.077
It was definitely a dramatic story.

89
00:04:26.918 --> 00:04:29.420
But Henry still wasn't convinced that it was true.

90
00:04:30.261 --> 00:04:35.064
That funny feeling inside him was stronger than ever, and he needed time to think about it.

91
00:04:35.084 --> 00:04:38.747
"Maggie he started to say.

92
00:04:38.767 --> 00:04:44.872
"That's when you made your plan," Maggie went on, glaring at Nathan and ignoring Henry.

93
00:04:45.712 --> 00:04:49.636
"You walked over and bought some lemonade for yourself and Nora.

94
00:04:50.416 --> 00:04:52.158
You even borrowed money from Mrs.

95
00:04:52.238 --> 00:04:53.579
Martin to pay for it!"

96
00:04:53.599 --> 00:04:55.020
"They did?"

97
00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:56.481
Henry was surprised.

98
00:04:57.282 --> 00:04:58.243
He hadn't known that.

99
00:04:59.504 --> 00:05:01.366
Maggie was still staring at Nathan.

100
00:05:01.386 --> 00:05:06.510
"Then you started talking to me, distracting me on purpose.

101
00:05:07.411 --> 00:05:12.495
That gave your sneaky little sister time to grab the money out of the cashbox while my back

102
00:05:12.535 --> 00:05:13.196
was turned.

103
00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:18.103
Then all she had to do was hide it and pretend she didn't know anything.

104
00:05:19.044 --> 00:05:23.588
I think she—" "Hold on, Maggie," Henry interrupted.

105
00:05:23.608 --> 00:05:26.791
"I just realized something.

106
00:05:27.711 --> 00:05:29.473
Nora couldn't have taken your money."

107
00:05:30.454 --> 00:05:34.617
Maggie, Cole, Nathan, and even Nora all turned to stare at him.

108
00:05:34.637 --> 00:05:37.319
"What are you talking about, Henry?"

109
00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:38.300
Maggie said.

110
00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:40.362
"Of course she did!

111
00:05:41.303 --> 00:05:42.704
Who else could have done it?"

112
00:05:43.672 --> 00:05:44.292
"I don't know."

113
00:05:44.893 --> 00:05:45.673
Henry shrugged.

114
00:05:45.693 --> 00:05:47.834
"But it wasn't Nora.

115
00:05:48.994 --> 00:05:49.995
You said it yourself.

116
00:05:50.935 --> 00:05:53.696
All she had to do was hide that money after she took it."

117
00:05:53.716 --> 00:05:56.237
"Right," Maggie said.

118
00:05:56.257 --> 00:05:59.719
"So?" "So don't you see?"

119
00:06:00.079 --> 00:06:01.099
Henry continued.

120
00:06:01.119 --> 00:06:05.561
"She couldn't hide it because she had nowhere to put it.

121
00:06:06.301 --> 00:06:12.384
Remember? Nora and Nathan stopped by the lemonade stand on their way home from the swimming pool.

122
00:06:13.330 --> 00:06:15.362
All they had on were their bathing suits!"
